    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present No. 6 St Anne's Road South to the market, a substantial and distinctive end-of-terrace period residence occupying a superb position immediately adjacent to the Grand Canal in one of Dublin 8's most established and sought-after residential neighbourhoods.\n\nExtending to approximately 155 sq. m., this impressive home offers exceptionally generous and versatile accommodation, comprising five bedrooms, five bathrooms and two well-proportioned reception rooms. The end-of-terrace position, together with its quiet setting and proximity to the canal, gives the property a wonderful sense of privacy and tranquillity while remaining within easy reach of Dublin city centre.\n\nA particularly interesting aspect of No. 6 is its history. The property was the first house built on St Anne's Road South, with the original builder himself residing in the house until the early 1950s. The property was also operated as a B&B for a number of years, adding further to its unique history and helping to explain the generous and versatile accommodation available throughout.\n\nWhile the property would now benefit from some modernisation, its substantial proportions, excellent accommodation and superb setting provide an exciting opportunity for a new owner to create a truly exceptional family home. The existing layout offers considerable flexibility and scope to reimagine the accommodation to suit modern family living.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from valuable off-street parking together with a garage, a significant advantage in this highly convenient city location. Its position beside the canal provides a peaceful setting and immediate access to the canal-side walking and cycling routes.\n\nThe property has also benefited from a number of recent upgrades, including the replacement of the oil tank and boiler in 2025 and the immersion heater downstairs in 2024.\n\nSt Anne's Road South is a quiet and established residential enclave, yet enjoys an enviable location close to the wealth of amenities that Dublin 8 and the South Circular Road have to offer. The area is particularly well served by a range of cafés, restaurants, schools, parks and excellent transport links. Dublin City is within easy reach with Grafton Street, Stephen's Green and Trinity College all within 20 minutes walk. \n\nProperties offering this combination of substantial accommodation, off-street parking, a garage, canal-side setting and such an interesting history are rarely available to the market. No. 6 St Anne's Road South represents an exciting opportunity to acquire a truly distinctive Dublin 8 residence and, with modernisation, create an exceptional family home in a peaceful and highly convenient city location."
      },
